<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaspard de Coligny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1519–1572</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Admiral Coligny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaspard de Coligny was a French nobleman, admiral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a>. He backed overseas Protestant colonies, supporting Villegaignon's France Antarctique in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1555 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-ribault">Jean Ribault</a>'s settlements in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> from 1562. He was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in August 1572 at the start of the St Bartholomew's Day massacre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaspard-de-coligny.jpg" alt="Gaspard de Coligny" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois_Clouet_-_Admiral_Gaspard_II_de_Coligny_-_168-1925_-_Saint_Louis_Art_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
